{"reference":"2 Chronicles 6","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Solomon’s Dedication Prayer","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Within 2 Chronicles 1–7, Solomon’s wisdom and temple building are portrayed as completing David’s preparations. This chapter’s public prayer belongs to that larger presentation, following the ark’s arrival and leading into the temple’s dedication, celebration, and the divine promise and warning that follow.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 6:12-42"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_006_05d0f41a27ada5f7280ab7b7"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}